 ## Subtopics
 
 ### Valley Cell Hierarchy Construction
-This variant constructs a tree structure representing the hierarchy of features by reversing the simplification process. It starts with the simplified valley cells and merges them in order of increasing boundary persistence (the reverse of the simplification order). When two cells are merged, parent-child relationships are established, and the maximum sets and boundary persistences of remaining boundaries are updated. The root of the resulting tree corresponds to the cell containing the largest local maximum. This hierarchy allows for interactive merging and splitting of features [S1].
